This target has desktop GL linked in: no loader, and no GLES

Two arms in `libultraship`'s SDL/GL backends pick how OpenGL arrives, and this
platform is a case neither of them has. Both are narrowed on `__PROSPERO__`, so
every other platform keeps exactly what upstream gave it.

**`glewInit()` - nothing to load.** `gfx_opengl.cpp:677` calls GLEW on every
platform except Linux and OpenBSD, because elsewhere the GL entry points past
1.1 have to be fetched from the driver at run time. Here they do not exist to be
fetched: `oops-gl` *is* the GL, it is linked into the payload, and every name is
an ordinary symbol the linker resolved. There is no driver to ask and no GLEW to
ask it with. This joins the list of platforms that already skip it, for the same
reason those two are on it.

**`SDL2/SDL_opengles2.h` - the wrong GL.** `gfx_sdl2.cpp`'s `#else` arm is
written for a Linux desktop, where SDL's GLES2 header is present. This target
has desktop GL and no GLES at all, so that include fails at
`GLES2/gl2platform.h` before anything else is parsed.

The new arm is placed *before* the `#else` rather than folded into it: the
existing branch means "a Unix with SDL's GLES2 headers", which stays true, and a
platform that answers differently is a new case rather than an exception inside
an old one. `<GL/gl.h>` is `oops-gl`'s own header, and `GL_GLEXT_PROTOTYPES` is
kept for the same reason the branch beside it keeps it.

Note what is deliberately *not* patched: the vertex-array pair at :683 stays
inside `#if defined(__APPLE__) || defined(USE_OPENGLES)`, because this port
genuinely does not call it. The vertex array objects `oops-gl` needs come from
ImGui's GL3 backend, which is a different library - see `../../oops-deps/imgui`.

diff --git a/libultraship/src/fast/backends/gfx_opengl.cpp b/libultraship/src/fast/backends/gfx_opengl.cpp
index c0746d3..0eb40e3 100644
--- a/libultraship/src/fast/backends/gfx_opengl.cpp
+++ b/libultraship/src/fast/backends/gfx_opengl.cpp
@@ -674,7 +674,7 @@ void GfxRenderingAPIOGL::DrawTriangles(float buf_vbo[], size_t buf_vbo_len, size
 }
 
 void GfxRenderingAPIOGL::Init() {
-#if !defined(__linux__) && !defined(__OpenBSD__)
+#if !defined(__linux__) && !defined(__OpenBSD__) && !defined(__PROSPERO__)
     glewInit();
 #endif
 
diff --git a/libultraship/src/fast/backends/gfx_sdl2.cpp b/libultraship/src/fast/backends/gfx_sdl2.cpp
